WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:05.400
The fallout from the Johnny Depp/Amber Heard&nbsp;
trial continues, and now its effects are even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:10.240
reverberating…under the sea. Well, kind&nbsp;
of. Here's what fans have learned from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.000
court filings about the behind-the-scenes&nbsp;
tension on "Aquaman and the Lost Kingdom."

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.160
Things haven't been great for&nbsp;
the DC Extended Universe lately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:22.200
and the same can be said for "Aquaman and&nbsp;
the Lost Kingdom" star Amber Heard. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.800
"Blue Beetle" bombed at the box office, the&nbsp;
DCEU is riding a four-movie failure train&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.560
toward the "Aquaman" sequel. Meanwhile,&nbsp;
Heard has spent much of the last few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:35.000
years in a series of highly public legal&nbsp;
battles with former partner Johnny Depp.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:41.040
As the Snyderverse era is nearing its end, both&nbsp;
Heard and the DCEU would no doubt welcome a win.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:45.960
However, potentially muddying the waters for&nbsp;
both is a new report by Variety, which contains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:51.480
some serious and occasionally strange allegations&nbsp;
about the production and its treatment of Heard.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.640
We should point out that the Variety article&nbsp;
doesn't contain direct quotes from Heard or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:59.920
other named parties. Instead, much of its&nbsp;
information stems from notes that were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:05.640
taken by her therapist, Dr. Dawn Hughes, during&nbsp;
sessions, as well as unnamed industry sources.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:08.360
These files first surfaced on Reddit in September,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:12.800
after Depp's fans paid for the release of court&nbsp;
documents. It's also worth noting that because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:18.240
the article was published during the ongoing&nbsp;
2023 SAG-AFTRA strike, neither Heard nor Momoa&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:22.000
can currently address the allegations to&nbsp;
the press. This means that at present,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.360
there's no way to know for certain what was,&nbsp;
or wasn't, said when these notes were taken.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:30.600
According to the article's allegations,&nbsp;
multiple people behind "Aquaman and the Lost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:35.553
Kingdom"—including director James Wan—wanted&nbsp;
Heard out because of her legal battles.

00:01:35.553 --> 00:01:41.680
"Sometimes you have to do what's right,&nbsp;
even if your heart aches against it."

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:45.360
The biggest bombshell in the new allegations&nbsp;
are the notes implying that "Aquaman 2"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:49.560
star Jason Momoa wanted to get rid of&nbsp;
Heard and was very much against her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:53.520
to the point of taunting her while dressed&nbsp;
like Depp. These notes allege that Heard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:58.685
described Momoa as, quote, "drunk, late&nbsp;
on set" and "Dressing like Johnny Depp."

00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:00.159
"Don't! No!"

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:04.520
These allegations are in clear conflict with&nbsp;
earlier claims that Momoa fought to keep Heard in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:09.960
"Aquaman 2." In all likelihood, we'll have to wait&nbsp;
until the SAG-AFTRA strike ends before Momoa's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:15.000
people comment on the situation, but for the&nbsp;
time being, insiders have vehemently denied these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:20.680
allegations, stating that Heard and Momoa had a&nbsp;
good relationship on the set. One source said,

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:24.720
"Jason works his ass off, likes to have&nbsp;
a beer once in a while like everyone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.480
but doesn't show up drunk to&nbsp;
set. And he isn't dressing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:31.120
like Johnny Depp. He has always&nbsp;
dressed in that bohemian style."

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:36.520
A DC representative has also denied the&nbsp;
allegations and praised Momoa's professionalism.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:39.280
Similarly, the studio has&nbsp;
also denied the allegations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:42.520
against James Wan. A spokesperson told Variety,

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:46.720
"James is known for treating members of his&nbsp;
cast and crew with the utmost respect and for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:52.120
fostering a positive, collaborative environment&nbsp;
on set — the 'Aquaman' films were no exception."

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:56.120
According to multiple sources, Warner Bros.&nbsp;
wasn't originally going to include Amber&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:01.040
Heard in "Aquaman and the Lost Kingdom," citing&nbsp;
chemistry issues with Momoa. Strangely enough,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:04.320
the notes allege that the reason she&nbsp;
ended up in the movie was none other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:07.960
than Heard's former partner Elon&nbsp;
Musk, who contacted Warner Bros.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:11.909
and threatened litigation should&nbsp;
Heard not be part of "Aquaman 2."

00:03:11.909 --> 00:03:15.709
"I'm going to kill Aquaman&nbsp;
and everything he holds dear."

00:03:15.709 --> 00:03:20.960
However, all of this reportedly happened in 2018&nbsp;
and was unconnected to the Heard-Depp trial.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:23.920
Due to the timing of the Variety article, Momoa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:28.880
Heard, and other parties may only be able&nbsp;
to comment on the news extremely belatedly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:33.480
if at all. Musk hasn't shared his version of&nbsp;
the events, either. As such, there's a chance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:38.000
that the notes and the allegations they contain&nbsp;
will resurface in the news somewhere downstream.

